From zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu  Fri Jan 15 14:44:47 1999
From: zaslavsk at hcp.med.harvard.edu (Alan Zaslavsky)
Date: Fri, 15 Jan 1999 09:44:47 -0500
Subject: Re: [S] Splus batch files
Message-ID: <199901151444.JAA16639@nightingale.med.harvard.edu>

lhw at umds.ac.uk (Mrs Lesley Wise) asks:
> I have a UNIX shell program which calls an Splus batch file. However,
> the shell program carries on without waiting for the batch program to
> finish. I have tried using the wait command in the UNIX shell
> program, but this doesn't seem to help.

If you look at $SHOME/cmd/BATCH you see the following:

#!/bin/shh
case $#
in
2)      BATCH=yes; export BATCH
        S_BATCH_INPUT=$1; S_BATCH_OUTPUT=$2; export S_BATCH_INPUT 
S_BATCH_OUTPUT        (echo "invisible(options(echo=TRUE))"; cat $1)| nohup 
Splus >$2 2>&1 &
        ;;
*)      echo "Usage: Splus BATCH inputfile outputfile"
        ;;
esac

If you copy this file and remove the "&" at the end of the line you
get a version of BATCH that waits until Splus finishes executing.
