sheet file (.sgr) is opened:

The Group item moniker you specified is not valid. Group item monikers must
be of the form [object type][path name of object].

Additionally, a blank graphsheet is displayed. I'm using S-PLUS 4.5 Rel 2
under NT 4.0 (SP4). I've also had this happen with S-PLUS 4.0.

The problem seems to be related to the format of the filename for the saved
graphsheet. For example, I created a simple graph and saved it as the
default of GS1.sgr and was able to reopen it just fine. However, resaving
that graphsheet as "GS1 test.sgr" (notice embedded blank space) caused the
error; reopening and resaving GS1.sgr as "GS1testfile.sgr" (removing the
blank and lengthening the filename) caused no problem. No problem occurred
reopening saved graphsheets with longer filenames or with underscores or
periods in the name. It seems that the embedded blank may be what is causing
the problem.

