>      SYSTAT nonlinear least squares parameter estimates are similar to 
>      those from SAS glm but SYSTAT standard errors are more similar to 
>      S-plus glm standard errors.  Great discrepancy between SAS/SYSTAT b0 
>      estimate and that of S-Plus is disturbing.

Have these converged? Try changing the control tolerances to be sure. Often
the likelihood surface is very flat if you have highly related or
ineffective carriers, and the convergence criterion in glm() is rather lax.
Actually, I don't see that a difference of less than 5% of an s.e. should
disturb you.

